option.AURELIA_ADAPTIVE.comment=Smooths prior-frame time with slow recovery. Master switch for Adaptive shadow filtering, its only consumer; off means a fixed shadow filter.
option.AURELIA_SHADOWS.comment=Reload-bound. Potato disables the map completely.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_RESOLUTION.comment=Reload-bound square depth allocation. Adaptive keeps this allocation fixed.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_DISTANCE.comment=Reload-bound caster and receiver coverage distance in blocks.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_FILTER_MAX.comment=Shadow-map reads use hardware-compared filtering. 1 takes one filtered read, 2 takes two (smoother diagonal edges), 3 takes four (a softer tent), dropping to two or one while Adaptive shadow filtering is short of frame-time headroom.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=Only attenuates direct sunlight; cool ambient and block light stay visible.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_ADAPTIVE.comment=Adaptive profile only. Only matters at Maximum shadow filter 3. Uses the smoothed frame-time signal to choose between one and four filtered reads without resizing the map.
option.AURELIA_WATER_SURFACE.comment=Physical water: wave normals, Fresnel reflection of the sky (and the scene with screen-space reflections), a sun glint, and light absorbed and scattered by the water column. Off draws water like glass.
option.AURELIA_WATER_ANIMATED.comment=The waves drift with time. ALU and texture reads only; Potato and Low keep the surface still.
option.AURELIA_WATER_DEPTH.comment=Reads the opaque depth behind the water (depthtex1) to measure the water column, so shallows are clear and deep water turns blue-green and dark. Off assumes three blocks.
option.AURELIA_WATER_SHORE.comment=A faint broken foam line where the water meets a wall or bank. Uses the same depth read.
option.AURELIA_WATER_UNDERWATER.comment=When the camera is submerged, everything fades into the water column's own colour, lit by the sun and sky above, and the surface shows Snell's window from below.
option.AURELIA_CLOUDS_SOFT.comment=Dissolved cloud edges, denser-core shading, a warm sun-side rim at low sun and a darker desaturated rain response, all ALU only on the vanilla cloud slab. Potato keeps the simplest treatment.
option.AURELIA_EXPOSURE.comment=Scene exposure applied before the filmic curve. 1.00 is the neutral baseline; higher values brighten the whole image.
option.AURELIA_CONTRAST.comment=Micro-contrast applied about mid-grey after the filmic curve. 1.00 is the neutral baseline; higher values deepen shadows and lift highlights.
option.AURELIA_DEBUG_VIEW.comment=Lighting shows normal and lightmap data. Frame pacing shows red pressure, green quality, blue reference. Raw shadow map displays depth. Shadow factor displays applied direct-light visibility. Adaptive shadow quality: red, amber, green are the low, middle and top adaptive tiers; only the top tier takes four reads (at Maximum shadow filter 3).
option.AURELIA_DISTANT_RAIN.comment=EXPERIMENTAL, off in every preset: adds a procedural two-layer distant-rain curtain on the final pass. Native Minecraft weather already surrounds the player, so this stays an experiment for manual testing only.
option.AURELIA_DISTANT_RAIN_LAYERS.comment=EXPERIMENTAL: number of curtain layers when the distant-rain curtain is enabled. 1 is cheapest, 2 is the tuned default.
option.AURELIA_FOLIAGE_TRANSLUCENCY.comment=Wrapped transmission for thin geometry: leaves and grass facing away from the sun pick up a little sunlight when you look sunward, instead of going black. Costs a few ALU ops and no texture read; it does not touch the shadow term.
profile.comment=Potato disables shadows, sky treatment, water effects and soft clouds. Low is a 512 map at 64 blocks with the water surface only. Balanced targets the M1 Air with a 1024 map at 96 blocks and every water effect. Cinematic uses a 1536 map at 128 blocks with the four-read shadow filter. Adaptive keeps a 1024 map fixed and changes only the shadow filter budget.
option.AURELIA_CLOUD_LAYER.comment=A soft, lit cloud layer drawn in the sky itself (procedural, sky pixels only) in place of Minecraft's blocky clouds. Turn off to get vanilla clouds back.
option.AURELIA_SHADOW_CASTERS.comment=Reload-bound. Which mobs, players and block entities (chests, signs, item frames) cast sun shadows. Each caster is an extra draw in the shadow pass; Player only is far cheaper in busy towns.
option.AURELIA_WAVING=Waving plants
option.AURELIA_WAVING.comment=Grass, flowers, double plants and leaves sway in the wind, stronger in rain. Vertex-only: no texture read or extra pass; leaf shadows sway with the leaves.
option.AURELIA_WAVING_STRENGTH=Wind strength
option.AURELIA_WAVING_STRENGTH.comment=How far plants and leaves sway. Rain adds up to 80% more.
option.AURELIA_OPAQUE_ICE=Opaque ice
option.AURELIA_OPAQUE_ICE.comment=Plain ice is drawn as a solid block instead of a translucent one: cheaper (no blending or sorting), and frozen lakes stop showing the water under them. Packed and blue ice are already opaque.
option.AURELIA_WET_SURFACES=Wet surfaces and puddles
option.AURELIA_WET_SURFACES.comment=In rain, ground under open sky darkens, puddles collect and grow as it keeps raining, and they reflect the sky with rain ripples and a sun glint; they dry out after the rain. Terrain only. Costs nothing in dry weather.
option.AURELIA_LENS_FLARE=Lens flare
option.AURELIA_LENS_FLARE.comment=Glare, a light streak and lens ghosts when the sun is on screen, fading as terrain covers it. Visibility is measured once per frame, so the cost is a little ALU in the final pass.
option.AURELIA_LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH=Lens flare strength
option.AURELIA_LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the whole lens flare.
option.AURELIA_FOG_HAZE=Height fog and sun haze
option.AURELIA_FOG_HAZE.comment=Fog is thickest near the ground and thins with altitude (never below 35%), and looking toward the sun the haze takes on the sky's warm glow so distant terrain blends into the sky. Evaluated per vertex: no per-pixel cost.
option.AURELIA_CLOUD_HIGH=High cirrus clouds
option.AURELIA_CLOUD_HIGH.comment=A second, thin and streaky cloud layer far above the painted clouds, drifting on its own wind. Needs the painted cloud layer. Two texture reads on sky pixels only.
option.AURELIA_GOD_RAYS=God rays
option.AURELIA_GOD_RAYS.comment=Light shafts from the sun through gaps in trees and buildings, traced through the depth buffer in the final pass (16 reads per pixel while the sun is up and near the frame). Cinematic by default.
option.AURELIA_GOD_RAYS_STRENGTH=God ray strength
option.AURELIA_GOD_RAYS_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the light shafts.
option.AURELIA_BLOOM=Bloom
option.AURELIA_BLOOM.comment=Bright light (the sun, sky, lamps) softly glows into its surroundings. Built from the scene's mip chain: no extra buffer or pass, about 16 texture reads per pixel. Cinematic by default.
option.AURELIA_BLOOM_STRENGTH=Bloom strength
option.AURELIA_BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment=How much of the glow is mixed in.
option.AURELIA_SHARPEN=Sharpening
option.AURELIA_SHARPEN.comment=Contrast-adaptive sharpening: crisper block textures without halos. Four texture reads per pixel. Useful at lower window resolutions.
option.AURELIA_SHARPEN_STRENGTH=Sharpening strength
option.AURELIA_SHARPEN_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly edges are sharpened.
option.AURELIA_SUN_PATH_ROTATION.comment=Tilts the sun's arc toward the south, as at mid latitudes, so noon light comes from an angle and shadows have direction. 0 is vanilla's overhead arc.
option.AURELIA_CITY_GLOW.comment=A faint warm skyglow near the horizon at night, the light pollution over a lit city. Adds to the sky texture once per frame; no per-pixel cost.
option.AURELIA_MATERIALS.comment=Gives blocks a physical surface from their ID: glossy metal, polished stone, glass, waxy leaves, emissive lamps. Needs no resource pack; ALU only.
option.AURELIA_SSR.comment=Glossy floors, metal, glass and water reflect the scene on screen, not just the sky. One screen-space march per glossy pixel; the main cost of High profiles.
option.AURELIA_SSR_STEPS.comment=Samples per reflection ray. More finds thin objects and long reflections; fewer is faster.
option.AURELIA_WATER_REFRACTION.comment=Water bends the view of the bed and tints it per colour through the water column, red first, from the opaque scene copy. Off blends the water over the bed in grey.
option.AURELIA_AUTO_EXPOSURE.comment=The camera adapts to the scene like an eye: bright noon, dark interiors and night all read. Off uses a fixed exposure from the sky light.
option.AURELIA_PURKINJE.comment=In very dim light colours fade and shift toward blue, as night vision does. Only affects scenes near darkness.
